---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Support CGP — Donations"
  description="Support the open development of the Context Governance Protocol through GitHub Sponsors."
>
  <section class="donation-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Open-source funding</span>
    <h1>Fund infrastructure that keeps AI context private and accountable.</h1>
    <p>
      CGP is being developed as an open protocol, open reference implementation and public conformance layer. Sponsorship helps keep the core auditable, independent and accessible.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="donation-layout">
    <article class="sponsor-card">
      <span class="section-label">GitHub Sponsors</span>
      <h2>Support the project directly.</h2>
      <p>
        Donations are processed through GitHub Sponsors on the maintainer profile. GitHub shows the available one-time and recurring sponsorship options for your account and region.
      </p>
      <a class="button button-sponsor" href="https://github.com/sponsors/MrQwenty" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        Sponsor CGP on GitHub →
      </a>
      <p><small>Payments, receipts and cancellation are managed by GitHub Sponsors.</small></p>
    </article>

    <article class="donation-panel">
      <span class="section-label">What funding supports</span>
      <h2>Public engineering work, not a closed protocol.</h2>
      <ul class="fund-list">
        <li><strong>Protocol specifications</strong><br />Schemas, RFCs, compatibility rules and implementation guidance.</li>
        <li><strong>Reference implementation</strong><br />Gateway, privacy processing, context planning, receipts and adapters.</li>
        <li><strong>Security and privacy</strong><br />Threat modelling, fuzzing, adversarial document testing and leak benchmarks.</li>
        <li><strong>Interoperability</strong><br />Conformance fixtures, independent implementations and provider integrations.</li>
        <li><strong>Documentation</strong><br />Examples, architecture material, onboarding guides and release documentation.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="transparency">
    <span class="section-label">Funding principles</span>
    <h2>Open core. Clear boundaries. No false promises.</h2>
    <div class="transparency-grid">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-number">01</span>
        <h3>The protocol stays inspectable</h3>
        <p>Specifications, schemas, baseline conformance and the reference core are intended to remain public and auditable.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-number">02</span>
        <h3>Sponsorship does not buy control</h3>
        <p>Funding supports development. It does not allow a sponsor to silently redefine compatibility, security or compliance semantics.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="card-number">03</span>
        <h3>Claims remain evidence-based</h3>
        <p>CGP will not claim automatic legal compliance, perfect anonymization or superiority without reproducible evidence.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="cta-panel">
      <div>
        <h2>Contribute in more than one way.</h2>
        <p>Code, documentation, review, testing, security research and sponsorship all help CGP mature.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/sponsors/MrQwenty">Donate through GitHub</a>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/project/contributing/">Contribution guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
